  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThe HTML spec may benefit from normative guidance on using the most appropriate type for IDL attributes. \n\nFor example, as part of a [recent ARIA-motivated update to the DOMString? getter](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/10974), @domenic called out that `DOMString?` may need to be discouraged for non-enumerated attributes. @annevk also agreed that general clarity on attribute design would be beneficial, so this issue would not be limited to `DOMString?` usage recommendations. ",
